### Test GPS Receiver API
### Install REST Client extension di VS Code untuk menggunakan file ini

# Variables
@supabaseUrl = https://your-project.supabase.co
@avl = your-device-avl
@apiKey = your-device-api-key

### Test 1: Send valid GPS data
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/functions/v1/gps-receiver
avl: {{avl}}
api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lat": -6.200000,
  "lng": 106.816666,
  "date_time": 1697644800000
}

### Test 2: Missing AVL header (should fail)
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/functions/v1/gps-receiver
api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lat": -6.200000,
  "lng": 106.816666,
  "date_time": 1697644800000
}

### Test 3: Invalid credentials (should fail)
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/functions/v1/gps-receiver
avl: invalid-avl
api-key: invalid-key
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lat": -6.200000,
  "lng": 106.816666,
  "date_time": 1697644800000
}

### Test 4: Invalid lat/lng range (should fail)
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/functions/v1/gps-receiver
avl: {{avl}}
api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lat": 200.0,
  "lng": 300.0,
  "date_time": 1697644800000
}

### Test 5: Invalid data format (should fail)
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/functions/v1/gps-receiver
avl: {{avl}}
api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lat": "not-a-number",
  "lng": "not-a-number",
  "date_time": "not-a-number"
}

